Father Józef Witko: I saw Jesus in a white robe
He's charismatic.
At the Holy Mass he celebrates for release and healing, they draw crowds.
He was a dozen years old when inexplicable things began to happen in his life.
Today, through the Franciscan, others experience it.
The Holy Masses celebrated by Father Witko for release and healing are drawn by crowds
It used to be attended by parents of a 7-month-old baby, who had in his heart a hole of 7.5 mm.
It's supposed to be operated on.
Father Joseph Witko prayed for him.
Later that day, the boy was taken to the hospital for surgery.
Amazed doctors said: "Surgery is not needed, the cavity is only 1.5 mm."
My parents cried with happiness.
After another prayer, the Franciscanne’s hole completely disappeared.
The clergyman began to experience the extraordinary actions of the Creator as a teenager.
In his dreams came to him purgatory souls asking for help.
"I was woken up at night and urged to pray for the dead and those who died at the moment," he recalls.
He also experienced the presence of an evil spirit.
And he had a vision of what happens to a man who commits a mortal sin.
“My body began to change.
“I lost people’s qualities and began to take on the appearance of an animal,” he says.
Invisible force lifted it up, he couldn't get his voice out.
He felt he'd been lost.
That's when God gave him salvation.
“Immersed in the waters of a river symbolizing holy baptism, I was freed and returned to the human form...”
He didn't tell anyone about these strange experiences.
His vocation matured in him.
He was 16 years old when he joined the Franciscans.
In the sermons, he didn’t just want to talk about Jesus.
He wanted people to experience him alive.
Members of the charismatic community of Renewal in the Holy Spirit
Masses for the healing celebrated by Witko’s father are attended by many people who are counting on getting rid of the disease.
However, the priest emphasizes that their main goal is spiritual healing, not bodily healing.
The first defeat of Kolping FRAC Jaroslaw
Today (26 September this year), the Kolping FRAC team deserved the current Polish Dartom champion Bogoria Grodzisk Mazowiecki as part of the 3rd LOTTO Superleague of Table Tennis.
In such a personal juxtaposition as they presented with Grodziszczans, they have a slim chance of victories against the league’s sovereigns.
This was clearly demonstrated by a duel with Dartom Bogoria.
The team is still lacking Chen Jingqi.
Perhaps with him in the line-up Yaroslavians would reach for a third consecutive triumph in the new season.
I don't think the young Asian Qiyao Han has yet grown into winning against such tusks as the Greek Panagiotis Gionis or Czech Pavel Sirucek.
Not even with one of the most forward-thinking Poles, Mark Badowski.
The rider from Hellada was the biggest star of the duel in the MOSiR hall at Sikorskiego Street in Jarosław.
Both in the clash with Qiyao Hanen and Kou Lei, he was a class to himself.
After three duels, Kolping FRAC led 2:1.
Kou Lei probably played Marek Badowski, and Daniel Górak, after an exciting, five-set-long battle by Pavel Siruck.
After that, however, it was worse.
Gionis didn't give Lea a chance.
You could still hope to win for two points, but Qiyao Han didn't live up to Badowski.
There will be no additional research for seniors.
Why? Why?
According to Rafał Trzaskowski’s announcements, a program of free preventive examinations for seniors aged 70 and 80 was to be introduced in Warsaw.
However, the idea will not be implemented because it has not gained the approval of the Ministry of Health and its subordinated Agency for the Protection of Medical Technologies and Tariffs.
In justification, the agency explained that the target group had been poorly selected.
“The above actions may even result in the detectability of individual disease units, which may contribute to deepening difficulties in access to NFZ services and negatively affect the patient, causing anxiety and discomfort associated with a falsely positive test result,” they wrote.
The decision of the ministry is not understood by the president of the capital.
“Money is ours, we’ve provided money for it.
Only the government is afraid that if people get tested, then later they will go to the doctor, which is absurd, because it is about leading to a situation in which prevention can be done faster.
All specialists know that this helps when it comes to the burden of the health system, because it helps in the rapid detection of diseases and in a reliable approach to health.
The government here has a very strange position, which I do not understand," said Rafał Trzaskowski.
“It is difficult for me to imagine that expert specialists say: Let’s not investigate, because there will be longer queues with the doctor, and if such specialists advise the government, then I am not surprised that there is a health service in such a state,” he added.
Palestine responds to Israel: "We will break all agreements so far
Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas said Thursday at a session of the U.N. General Assembly that he would break any agreements with Israel if the country's future government tries to fulfill Benjamin Netanyahu's announcement of the annexation of the occupied Palestinian lands.
“If the future government of Israel that arises proceeds to implement this plan, we will invalidate all signed agreements (with Israel) and withdraw from all the commitments made,” he said.
"We're going to reject the whole plan completely and completely," Abbas threatened with emphasis.
"It is our duty to defend all our rights by all possible means - insignificant what the consequences will be - by engaging entirely in action for the application of international law and in the fight against terrorism," said the Palestinian Authority president, who had already made similar declarations in July.
Netanyahu, Israel's former prime minister, was once again given a mission to form a government after the September 17 election.
A week before the election, he announced that if he wins them, he will announce the annexation of the Jordan Valley and intend to include all Jewish settlements throughout the West Bank into Israel.
In the early 1990s, Israel and the Palestinians, led by Yaser Arafat at the time, signed a series of peace agreements patronized by the United States.
The 84-year-old Abbas also vowed during a session of the U.N. General Assembly to hold a general election on Palestinian lands.
The last took place in 2006.
"After returning to the country, I will convene in the West Bank, in the Gaza Strip and in East Jerusalem local elections, and everyone who opposes them will have to answer for their actions before God and the international community," the Palestinian president declared solemnly.
Abbas also defended, in his Speech, Palestine's rights, treated as a permanent observer at the United Nations, for the exercise of the powers of "full-fledged U.N. members and all its organs and institutions."
The Palestinian leader ended his speech with a call to the international community to "force Israel to fulfill in full respect of the United Nations."
Israeli Ambassador Danny Danon responded briefly to Abbas' speech, declaring that the Palestinian leader "would rather focus at the U.N
Danon, as the agencies noted, however, did not refer to Netanyahu's announced annexation of the occupied Palestinian lands.
Rescuers want defibrillators at the sensitive points of Przemysl
The history of the border crossing shows that an automatic AED defibrillator can save people's lives.
The Provincial Ambulance Station in Przemyśl wants such devices to end up in critical points of the city.
For their attitude, officers received congratulatory diplomas from the Provincial Ambulance Station in Przemyśl.
Applicant Daniel Cyrnek, senior applicant Grzegorz Bal and Commissioner Jacek Wójcik are officers of the Podkarpackie Tax Customs Office in Przemyśl.
On August 28, they served at the Polish-Ukrainian border crossing in Medyka. An officer of the Customs and Tax Service noticed an unconscious man in the pedestrian zone.
A Chinese activist has died in the custody of torture.
He wanted to take advantage of the rights guaranteed by the constitution
Cao Shuxia, the activist's wife, was called on September 23 by the Communist Party secretary from her home village to report that her husband had just passed away at a military hospital in Hengyang.
What was the cause of the death – he did not reveal.
In the morgue, Cao saw her husband's body massacred, unrecognizable.
“His eyes, ears, nose and lips were covered in blood,” the woman says.
“They wouldn’t let me take my cells with me, and there were a lot of cops around who didn’t get close to Wang.”
Police pressured them to sign a statement that her husband was seriously ill and died of an "unhappy accident."
105 million PLN for companies in the video game industry from the National Centre for Research and Development
Nearly 105 million zlotys of co-financing will go to companies from the gaming industry, creating innovative solutions.
On Friday, the National Centre for Research and Development announced the results of the 3rd edition of the GameINN program.
Among the nearly 30 projects supported by the NCBR were m.in. the development of a platform for the development of off-road games based on an AR game engine creating a map of the real world together with an application enabling the transmission of data by users; a test and training platform for verification of practical skills at the workplace and professional development with the use of VR and AI technology; an innovative game simulating the management of real production processes using an innovative gameplay model based on the virtual world
The aim of the GameINN sectoral programme is to increase the competitiveness of the Polish sector of video game producers on the global market in perspective until 2023.
According to NCBR, the Polish video gaming sector is already growing at an annual rate of 10%.
According to government data, the value of the Polish video game market in 2016 amounted to 1.85 billion PLN, while the forecast for 2019 was 2.23 billion.
“The specially prepared GameINN research agenda and already reaching 300 million zlotys of support for entrepreneurs under this sectoral program provide an important impulse for the further, dynamic growth of the Polish gamedev,” reads the release.
The video game industry is a perfect example of effective use of the potential that we have in Poland.
“The incentives introduced by the government for innovative entrepreneurs, such as R&D reliefs, competence improvement programs, IP box or support programs implemented by the NCBR drive the innovative activities of companies and allow them to compete more effectively in a very competitive market,” said Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Science and Higher Education Jarosław Gowin, quoted in the announcement.
The head of the Ministry of Science points out that the money for innovation not only goes to innovators in the form of co-financing projects, but also stays in their pockets – three-quarters more entrepreneurs took advantage of the R&D relief in 2018 than a year earlier.
“The amount of deducted costs related to R&D activities amounted to 1.7 billion zlotys, which gave more than 300 million zloty savings for companies benefiting from this relief.
This is the equivalent of support provided by NCBR in three GameINN editions," emphasizes the Deputy Prime Minister.
The NCBR’s director Wojciech Kamieniecki reminds that in the two previous competitions co-financing with a total value of over 211.2 million zlotys was awarded to 78 innovative projects.
Huge interest in the third competition and the variety of submitted applications show that the video game industry has ideas and competences to continue to develop and increase its competitive advantages.
“Particularly welcome is the fact that there are projects among the selected projects – as in previous editions – concerning solutions aimed not only for entertainment, but also related to industry 4.0,” he adds.
In the third GameINN competition, entrepreneurs, consortia of entrepreneurs and consortia with scientific units could apply for co-financing of up to 20 million zlotys.
NCBR received 87 applications for a total amount of co-financing approx. 317 million PLN.
The budget of the competition at the time of the announcement of the competition amounted to 100 million zlotys, but was increased, thanks to which 27 projects were awarded almost 105 million zlotys of funding.
Detailed information about the results of the 3rd GameINN competition is available at ncbr.gov.pl.
GameINN’s sectoral programme is implemented under the Smart Growth Operational Programme.
NCBR launched the program in 2016 in response to the initiative of entrepreneurs associated in the Polish Games Agreement, which includes m.in. such companies as CD Projekt, Techland, CI Games, Bloober Team or 11 bit studios.
Lamine Diaby-Fadiga pleads guilty to stealing Kasper Dolberg watch
The incident happened on September 16.
Dolberg, which in late Augustry made his way from Ajax Amsterdam to Nice, realized after training that his watch had disappeared from the locker room.
It's not just any, because it's worth 70 thousand euros.
Angry Dane the next day didn't show up in class, explaining his stomach problems.
The case has been puzzling from the beginning.
Players in the locker room have at their disposal private safes, and the club area is monitored.
According to the AFP news agency, Diaby-Fadiga eventually confessed.
The 18-year-old has already apologised to Dolberg and other team-mates and coach Patrick Vieira.
He also promised the Dane to return the money for his watch.
Diaby-Fadiga is one of the young generation's most forward-thinking players in France.
He went to Nice as a thirteen-year-old to make his first-team debut three years later.
He has featured in seven games this season.
He recently signed a professional contract, but – according to the newspaper L’Equipe – the club will probably solve it with immediate effect.
For now, he initiated disciplinary action against his player.
Nice, at least officially, refuses to comment on the matter.
See if you’re washing your hands well
We all know that they need to be washed (e.g. after coming home or before a meal).
But not everyone knows that in order to actually get rid of germs, you need to do it in the right way.
This is especially important right now, when autumn infections are approaching.
It takes at least 30-40 seconds to sufficiently remove dangerous bacteria and viruses from our hands
Most of us wash it shorter!
All you need is warm water and regular soap – it’s not true that it has to be antibacterial (many doctors even advise against it).
Washing, we rub not only the bottoms and tops of the hands, but also: the tips of the fingers (combined or individually) – rub them with circular movements against the interior of the other hand, the spaces between the fingers (intersperse your hands, rubbing your fingers against each other), thumbs – each thumb embraces the other hand and in such an embrace we spin it for a moment to the right and left.
In an emergency (when you can't wash your hands) you should wipe your hands with a wet handkerchief, and then use antibacterial gel (in drugstores, from 5 zł).
After using the public toilet, do not touch with washed door handles or doors (recommendation of the Chief Sanitary Inspectorate).
Open it through a paper towel.
Iran's president says he has rejected a proposal for talks with the U.S
Tehran did not hold talks with the U.S. party during the U.N. General Assembly in New York, despite the U.S. offer to lift sanctions, Iranian President Hassan Rouhani said on Friday.
U.S. President Donald Trump commented that it was the Iranian side who asked for the restrictions to be lifted, which he did not agree to.
According to Iranian President Hasan Rouhani, the U.S. proposed lifting all sanctions imposed on Tehran in exchange for entering into negotiations on a new international agreement.
It would regulate both Iran's nuclear agenda and a ballistic missile-building programme.
Rowhani: Iran won't take talks in an atmosphere of maximum pressure
Iran's president said he had refused to take up those talks due to a "toxic atmosphere."
He declared that he met with American diplomats because he succumbed to the encouragement of France, Germany and the United Kingdom.
However, he stressed that Iran would not hold talks in an atmosphere of "maximum pressure."
“And even if we want to negotiate with the Americans in 5+1 format, no one can predict what the end result will be,” Rowhani said.
A day earlier, the Iranian leader had said he did not rule out talks with the U.S., and accused the European sides of a nuclear deal in favor of U.S. sanctions on Iran.
He added that the sanctions imposed on Iran after the U.S. withdrawal from the nuclear deal "are a prerequisite that does not allow you" to establish dialogue.
If we can abolish this preliminary condition and if America abolishes sanctions and maximum pressure, then of course we can talk to America," he declared.
He added that he did not rule out a meeting with U.S. President Donald Trump, even though he did not agree to such a conversation last week at the U.N. General Assembly.
Trump: 'Iran asked, I said no'
Donald Trump tweeted that he was the one who rejected the Iranian side's request.
“Iran wanted me to lift the sanctions imposed on them so that we could meet.
Of course, I said “no!” tweeted by the President of the United States.
Tensions with atomic agreement in the background
France, Germany and the United Kingdom are trying to alleviate tensions between Washington and Tehran to save the 2015 Iran deal in some form, of which they were signatories.
It stipulated that in exchange for the abolition of economic sanctions, Iran would give up its nuclear weapons building program, and the nuclear sector would put the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) under scrutiny.
Since the U.S. withdrew from the agreement in May 2015, the other signatories have repeatedly confirmed that they want to keep the agreement in force.
So far, nothing has come of it.
Washington employs tactics to exert maximum pressure on Iran, and sanctions include a full embargo on Iranian oil.
Tehran announced that if he did not receive permission to export the raw material, every 60 days he would limit his obligations under the agreement.
HRUBIESZÓW: Kabaret near Wyrwigrosz
We've got tickets for you.
The cabaret near Wyrwigrosz will perform on October 6 at 6 a.m. at the Hrubieszów Cultural Centre in Hrubieszów.
The cabaret near Wyrwigrosz will present a program, titled "Tra this one."
There will be m.in. talks about pop-up beverages and Toruń geothermaly.
Tickets are 60 zł, you can buy them at HDK, as well as on the website biletowakasa.pl.
For TZ readers, we have free passes.
How to get them, check out our Facebook profile.
The judge of the Provincial Administrative Court in Warsaw and the husband of Emilia’s hater, whicho – according to her words and screenshots from WhatsApp – participated in stalking against judges, was restored on Wednesday to adjudication by the NSA.
The reason: disciplinary proceedings have not been initiated against him, so there is no basis for upholding the ordinance of WSA President Wojciech Mazur to remove him from his duties.
At the end of August, Judge Jerzy Chromicki, a disciplinary spokesman at the NSA, initiated an investigation against Szmydt at the end of August, but it has not yet turned into proceedings against him.
Although the NSA, which in such cases acts as a disciplinary court, has to deal with the decision of the WSA president within a month of its release.
In this situation, the judge, who publicly talked about his wife’s mental problems in order to discredit her, who, due to suspicions of participating in a hater group, was removed from the KRS office will return to adjudication and will issue judgments on behalf of the Republic of Poland.
Judge Szmydt denies his involvement in the hater group.
He argues there's no evidence for it other than the forged screenshots and the words of his wife he's getting divorced.
That’s exactly what the other “Casta” judges say: they’re all innocent, there’s no evidence.
And it's quite possible that they'll bet on their own.
Because the prosecutor's office didn't lift a finger to secure evidence from their electronic media, and it's also silent about the contents of Emilia Szmydt's phone, which the phone stopped in June in another case.
The police did not lift a finger to secure the devices of people whom Judge Waldemar Żurek pointed out as persecutors as persecutors in a report from February.
There is no evidence – there’s no Szmydt case, there’s no “Kasta” case.
There is also no matter of the head of NIK Marian Banaś about renting the tenement to the pimps and hiding income.
The CBA is reviewing his property statements.
He'll see when he's checked.
And the Committee on Deputie Ethics will not take care, because the Sejm is suspended (but the State Control Commission somehow gathered to make a bizarre decision to dismiss Banaś's deputies and appoint his lawyer, although the law does not provide for such a strange combination).
The whole thing reminds me of a movie novel, American I think, about how my wife comes home and finds her husband with her mistress in bed.
She's so amazed and devastated that she can't say a word.
She's standing at the door stunning, and at the time the mistress quickly jumps out of bed, dresses and walks out.
And the husband makes the bed.
When the wife regains her voice and shouts: what is this?
Who's that woman?
The husband calmly asks: what woman, darling?
Only in the case of "Caste" or Banasia there is a parody of the state.
And it's not funny at all.
