Kamila Lićwinko in the high jump final
Previously returning to the competition this season after the maternity break, the bronze medalist of the world championships from London 2017, in the first attempt defeated 1.85 and 1.89 and in the second 1.92.
1.94 managed to get it only in the third approach.
“I’m happy.
I showed that I can fight, because the first attempt was completely unsuccessful.
In the final, I will have to jump better technically," Lićwinko admitted in front of Eurosport's camera.
In the qualifiers the best turned out to be American Vashti Cunningham and Belarusian Karyna Demidik – after 1.94.
Both players were the only ones who did not lose any height.
The women's high jump final is scheduled for Monday.
Beginning at 19.30 Polish time.
Kornel Morawiecki is in hospital in a serious condition
He's taken to the hospital, and his doctors describe his condition as severe.
It should be added that he is conscious and conscious.
“We believe he’ll come out of this, that he’ll win again.
We are all praying for him to recover," Kornel Morawiecki's anonymous loved one said in an interview with “Super Express” reporters.
In the upcoming elections, the prime minister's father is running for the Senate.
“The closest family and politics keep me alive,” Kornel Morawiecki said in an interview he gave to Super-Express journalists two weeks ago.
In January, “Super Express” reported that 78-year-old Kornel Morawiecki went for examinations to the Military Hospital in Wrocław.
“I’ve had strange, disturbing symptoms and I’ve come to the hospital.
It's out that I have jaundice.
But the worst was in front of me
When a CT scan was performed, it was found that I had pancreatic cancer...” said the prime minister’s father.
A few days later at the MSWiA hospital in Warsaw, Kornel Morawiecki underwent major surgery.
As Morawiecki told, President Andrzej Duda sent his personal chaplain Father Zbigniew Kras to the hospital.
The operation lasted about three hours and proceeded successfully.
“I know that a lot of people prayed for me, thank you very much.
Fortunately, I don't have metastases.
I don't know if I'm going through chemotherapy yet.
I put myself in the hands of specialist doctors who are of a rather good thought.
For now, after this severe operation, I have to go back to some state of usability.
I hope that everything will be okay," Kornel Morawiecki said in January in an interview with "SE".
“If I underwent an examination too late, the situation would have been direty, and I would have said goodbye to it...” he added.
Krakow: 14-year-old missing
Officers from the Municipal Police Headquarters in Krakow are looking for 14-year-old Nel Stokłosy.
Anyone who has any information about the missing person is asked to contact us.
Missing on September 26 in the evening, she left her residence and has not yet returned, nor made contact with loved ones.
She was last seen at Stary Gościniec Street in Krakow.
Nel Stokłosa is 14 years old, measuring 167 cm, has blonde hair and gray-blue eyes.
The last time she was seen, she was dressed in a sweatshirt, gray trousers and shoes.
Anyone who has any information about the missing person is asked to contact the police at 12 61-52-911, 12 61-53-616 or 112, 997.
The power of Oława jumping.
The title of reports from amateur sports competitions, held on Sunday afternoon 15 September at the hippodrome at Oleandra Street in Oława, can be confusing for some.
There is a long way to true power, but this is the name of one of the types of horse competition...
The jumping power competition consists in overcoming by the rider and the horse ever higher obstacles, which in the most prestigious international competitions exceed up to two meters.
It is worth mentioning here that the long-standing and still unbeaten world record, established in 1949, by the Chilean Albert Larraguibel, on the horse "Huaso", is 247 cm.
Of course, nobody jumped so high in Oława, but the result of the best local amazons at the level of 135 cm is also not the worst...
Competitions organized by the tireless Jan Sienkiewicz and other JKS activists “In the saddle” were a demonstration part of the “Rainbow equestrian competitions”, about which we write more broadly in this issue of the newspaper, on page 22.
Eight amazons joined the competition, training equestrianism in Oława JKS.
Four competed on ponies and four on large horses.
In the first group Nikola Szołdra did the best, riding the crazy “Sprinter”.
This small, but very dynamic stallion began by overcoming obstacles spread out at a height of 40 cm, and he ended up only at the station with an upper beam away from the ground by 125 cm.
However, he did not give up easily and only after three consecutive refusals was removed from further competition by the jury of the competition.
The second place in pony jumps was taken by Amelia Pawlak, riding “Famy”, and the third by Lena Boruń on “Harmider”.
Ambitiously fought the youngest participant of the tournament - Inga Aksman, galloping and jumping through obstacles on a small mare "Carmen".
Even greater emotions were accompanied by the starting amazons and spectators during the competition with the participation of large horses.
Paulina Szewczyk, riding the “Declaration” and Anastasia Abramenko, who was going on “Lotka”.
Fortunately, apart from minor bruises, neither amazons nor horses, nothing bad happened, so they continued to participate in the competition.
A lot of problems with the introduction of the young mare “Wineta” to the parch had Weronika Łuczkiewicz riding her.
It was needed either the coach’s assist or another coaching horse, followed by a slightly crazy “Vineta”.
After passing the obstacle from the park, she also descended fully, so at times in the cubicles and at the expansion room it became dangerous. “Everything is under control!”, Jan Sienkiewicz calmed down a bit of frightened spectators, especially the youngest ones.
Since the beginning of the competition of large horses, Marta Masalska has performed well in the park, riding a beautifully presented “Whisky”.
This dignified mare, paired with an experienced amazon, followed by the second approach in the final phase was the first to jump 135 cm and this was the best result of the competition at the moment.
After a while, however, the same amount was also scored by Paulina Szewczyk on the “Declaration”, Weronika Łuczkiewicz on “Wineta” and Anastasia Abramenko on “Lotek”.
For the decoration of the flo and for the collection of in-kind prizes in the form of equestrian equipment, all these contestants left together, and at the end, together with amazons on ponies in Radecki’s march, they made an impressive round of honoraries, ending these interesting and exciting competitions.
Thanks
Equestrian Sports Club “W Sadło” sincerely thanks to the sponsors of the jumping power competition during the 16th “Rainbow Equestrian Competition”: the Municipal Office in Oława, the Department of Water and Sewagement in Oława, the District Office and the “Mustang” company.
Max Kolonko cuts off from KWW Max Kolonko's Patriotic Revolution
KWW The Patriotic Revolution of Max Kolonko is the name of the electoral committee under which the political formation #R Revolution of Mariusz Max Kolonka was to go to the October parliamentary elections.
The revolution directed its proposal especially to young voters with right-wing views.
Before the elections, Kolonko announced cooperation with Marek Jakubiak or Paweł Kukiz, but none of these coalitions took place, and KWW Patriotic Max Kolonko Revolution itself did not even manage to collect enough signatures to issue lists in any constituency in Poland.
Now Kolonko has tweeted that he has ceased cooperation with KWW The Patriotic Max Kolonko Revolution.
"I'm going to expect the above mentioned KWW to delete my name from the name.
I kindly ask you not to connect me with the above-mentioned entity”, he added and announced that he will provide more information soon.
For now, it is not known whether the journalist will continue his action, whether this is the end of the #R Revolution formation.
On July 4, American Independence Day, U.S. journalist Mariusz Max Kolonko announced the creation of a new political formation - #R Revolution.
In recent years, Kolonko has become famous for running the Max TV channel on YouTube, where he comments on events in Poland and around the world.
“We’ve had enough of the politicians, enough of your stupid games, enough of your amateur governments.
It is time that the authorities in the state take over the Nation and govern for the good of the Nation," Kolonko said at the time.
The party’s program includes issues related to the judiciary (it should be elected in general elections), tax changes (equation of the tax-free amount for all), war reparations (in the form of military assistance to NATO’s eastern flank countries, with particular emphasis on Poland), conducting a referendum on the possession of weapons, limiting the number of deputies or the introduction of single-member constituencies.
A few days after announcing the creation of a new political formation, Mariusz Max Kolonko joined the talks with Marek Jakubiak.
At the end of July, Kolonko posted on his social media profile an information suggesting that #R would join forces with the Kukiz'15 movement.
However, none of these coalitions eventually took place.
UBS: Golden close to equilib
“In the coming months, the euro exchange rate will remain around a ceiling of 4.35 zlotys, accompanied by a weak economic situation on global markets,” said Michael Bolliger from UBS Wealth Management.
“Expectations to maintain a solid pace of economic growth and a stable monetary policy speak in favor of stabilizing the zloty’s quotations at the current ceiling,” the specialist says in an interview with Bankier.pl.
In his opinion, despite clear inflationary pressures, the Monetary Policy Council will not decide on rate hikes in an environment in which the vast majority of central banks alleviate policy.
While the zloty is properly valued – euro quotations should remain in the coming months around the ceiling of 4.35 zlotys – according to him, Polish bonds are not attractive.
Much more favorable yields than Polish securities are offered bonds from emerging markets,” estimates Michael Bolliger, the head of asset allocation to emerging markets accompanied by UBS Wealth Management.
According to the specialist, the main threat to the Polish economy is the downturn in the world.
“The global slowdown may deepen even further, but there should be no severe recession, and at the same time there should be a slightly below-zero GDP momentum.”
“Investors should underestimate global stocks, which may be harmed by a lack of prospects for resolving U.S.-China trade conflict and other geopolitical risk factors, including Donald Trump’s impeachment procedure and Brexit.
Among the stock markets, Europe should behave relatively weakest," according to the latest letter to investors by UBS Wealth's chief executive Brand Haefele.
“Actions from eurozone countries should behave worsely than U.S. countries because they are more vulnerable in conditions of heightened uncertainty around global trade and fears of a slowdown,” the document reads.
According to Michael Bolliger, after the hossa in the bond markets of the safest countries pushed the yields of the German 10-yeasters even up to minus 0.74 per cent, it is still possible to deepen the decline in profitability.
However, in the long term, long-term paper yields should no longer fall, but only short-term, due to the mitigation of banks’ monetary policy.
The Fed has the biggest scope for rate cuts, which should lead to a weakening of the U.S. currency over the next years.
The long-term equilibrium point for euro quotations is the US$1.29 ceiling, which would mean a 19 per cent potential to strengthen the single currency for the dollar.
We look forward to further reductions in the Fed's rates, which will result in a decrease in differences in global monetary policies.
“Overrender deficits may not allow you to keep the strength of the dollar in the long term,” says Michael Bolliger.
The Bundeswehr loses its weapons.
Confidential report of the German Ministry of Defence
Since the beginning of 2014, the Bundeswehr has recorded the disappearance of 39 weapons, 39 parts of weapons and 19 445 rounds of ammunition – according to a confidential statement drawn up in the German defence ministry.
Information was provided by a press belonging to the media group RedaktionsNetzwerk Deutschland (RND).
According to a document coming from the parliamentary office of the secretary of state in the Ministry of Defense Peter Tauber (CDU), so far it has managed to re-trace two weapons, one part of weapons and 3474 ammunitions.
Among the military equipment that still remains missing, there are, among others, six universal MG3 machine guns, 11 G3 automatic rifles, four G36 automatic rifles, six signal guns and two P8 pistols.
In addition, there are 30 barrels for MG3 machine guns.
Vice-president Martina Renner expressed concern about the situation.
As she told RND reporters, the number of missing weapons and ammunitions is “perpetitive.”
All the more so because as a result of the ongoing investigations it was possible to find only a small part of lost equipment.
Martina Renner summarized the effects of these actions as a "wretched balance sheet."
She also criticized the fact that it did not appear from the statement whether there was also a weapon that was found there during an investigation against Bundeswehr lieutenant Franco A. In December 2017, the federal prosecutor's office in Karlsruhe accused him of preparing a grave act of violence threatening the security of the state and violating the provisions of a law regulating access to firearms.
The officer was accused of preparing assassinations on leading German politicians for far-right and racist reasons.
His “black list” of goals, which fell into the hands of the prosecutor’s office, included m.in. then-Justice Minister Heiko Maas of the SPD, Claudia Roth of the Green Party, and Anetta Kahane, human rights defender and founder of the Amadeu Antonio Stiftung foundation in Berlin.
Franco A. came illegally into the possession of four firearms, more than 1,000 ammunitions and more than 50 explosives.
Crying kids on a plane.
How do we avoid them?
There's a solution
Japan Airlines recently uses a function developed for people for whom traveling in the company of a crying child is a nightmare.
Through the website, the lines allow you to check the distribution of seats on the plane.
If a given call travels a minor until the age of two, then the “child icon” appears on a specific, reserved by parents or guardians of the seat.
Thus, the person using the services of the carrier has the opportunity to choose a place distant from that occupied by the toddler.
The BBC reports that the airlines have already announced the shortcomings of the solution.
“Child icon” will not appear if the ticket has been booked by a third party or if there has been a change of aircraft at the last minute.
As you might expect, the idea divided Internet users.
Some Twitter users point out that the problem of traveling with crying children can be solved with noise-reducing headphones.
They're kids, we used to be kids, too.
“We have to learn tolerance, because soon we’re going to start to need a map of seats for breathable lips, drooling or drunk,” wrote user G Sundar.
Another Internet user noticed that he was once disturbed by crying children on a plane, but he changed his mind when he became a parent himself.
There is also a shortage of supporters of the solution introduced by Japan Airlines.
“I thank you for warning me from screaming children on a 13-hour journey,” Rahat Ahmed wrote.
Majorca is counting losses after bankruption by travel agency Thomas Cook
More than 25,000 foreign tourists won't arrive on holiday to Majorca in October as a result of a bankruptcy announced on Monday by travel agent Thomas Cook.
According to Marc Pons, a representative of the Balearic Autonomous Balearic Government, among the 25,000 holidaymakers who won’t be able to take advantage of their October holiday in Majorca, there are also people who were expected to travel with companies indirectly associated with Thomas Cooke, e.g. Neckermann.
Pons explained that 80 per cent of expected holidaymakers, which, due to the bankruptcy of a British company, had to give up a holiday in Majorca next month are citizens of Germany and Scandinavian countries.
However, according to Pons, due to the fact that Thomas Cook did not direct tourists to the Balearic island in November-April, the losses for the local economy will be smaller.
He revealed that the Balearic government has already begun negotiations with international operators on "entry into the Majorca market" after the British operator's bankruption.
According to estimates of the Diario de Mallorca newspaper, more than 1,000 people will lose their jobs due to the tourism crisis in Mallorca in October.
Approximately 800 are laid-off employees of the Thomas Cook office in Palma.
Other people will lose their jobs mainly in the hospitality sector.
On Monday, along with the declaration of bankruptcy by Thomas Cook in a number of Mallorca hotels, the owners of the facilities demanded that the guests pay an additional fee for the accommodation.
Dozens of tourists from Poland have experienced this situation.
The Balearic government estimates that by Thursday, dozens of hotels in Majorca had halted operations at least until the end of October in connection with the declaration of bankruptcy by Thomas Cook and the companies cooperating with it.
In turn, Friday’s Diario de Ibiza newspaper points out that the majority of hotels operating in Ibiza, which cooperated with the Thomas Cook group, are not worn with the intention of closing outlets in the coming weeks.
The newspaper reminds that on this Baleric island the British bankrupt cooperated with 42 hotels.
On Wednesday, Balearic autonomous authorities announced that they would ask Spain's government to support the region with 100 million euros to cover losses caused by a bankruptcy by travel agent Thomas Cook.
They revealed that the most tourists injured in this archipelago, about 36,000 people, are located in Mallorca.
According to data from the Balearic government, Thomas Cook is in arrears of local tourism companies, mainly hotel operators, for the implementation of agreements for the July-September 2019 period about 5 million euros.
FIFA women's ranking.
Poland still in 29th place, the U.S. at the helm
The women's national team of Poland ranks 29th in the International Football Federation (FIFA) ranking published on Friday.
In the same position, the team of coach Miłosz Stępiński was ranked in the previous July ranking.
Weak squad matches.
How will it be in October?
