PZPN sprinkles penalties for brawls in stadiums.
Disqualified Griffin
The clash within the Polish Cup between Gryf Wejherowo and Lechia Gdańsk by a small hair did not end tragically, when the goalkeeper of the opposing team, Zlatan Alomerović, fired by fans from Wejherowo.
After this incident, the match was interrupted for 20 minutes.
The PZPN committee investigating this case imposed a severe penalty on Gryf, excluding him from future competitions.
The club will not be able to compete in the Polish Cup in the 2020/2021 season.
In addition, fans will not be allowed in the next match for their own stadium.
They will also not be able to leave in groups for league matches until December 31.
