Names of foreign cities on road signs also in Polish
GDDKiA plans to replace signage across its managed road network by the end of 2020.
GDDKiA Rzeszów
In Podkarpacie began the implementation of an amendment to the regulation of the Ministry of Infrastructure on m.in. to record the names of foreign cities on road signs also in Polish.
For example, "Lions" will appear next to "L'viv".
In our voivodship, changes will be introduced on 94 road signs set on the A4 motorway and national roads: DK19, DK94.
As we hear, it's supposed to be easier, clearer and simpler.
The new guidelines result from an amendment to the Regulation of the Minister of Infrastructure on detailed technical conditions for road signs and signals and road safety devices.
“We should remember that the names of towns in neighboring countries often also have Polish sound.
Thanks to the change prepared by us in the law, they will finally appear on the signposts on our roads.
Introduction of new signage begins with the Podkarpackie section of the A4 motorway,” said the Minister of Infrastructure Andrzej Adamczyk.
In Podkarpacie, changes will be introduced on 94 road signs set on the A4 motorway and national roads: DK19, DK94.
Total investment cost?
200 thousand zlotys.
In the first place, the new signage will be implemented on the A4 motorway, which is planned by November 1, 2019.
What should the implementation of the idea look like?
It will be done without replacing the boards, on the basis of pastes.
They will replace the currently functioning names of localities with new ones, written in Polish on already existing signs.
Both names will be saved in one poem – first in Polish, and then in the original, in brackets.
It will be a great convenience for people who do not know the spelling of the names of foreign cities in the language of the country where they are located.
Feel the game together with Razer Nari Ultimate for Xbox One
Razer has announced Razer Nari Ultimate for Xbox One, the world’s first headset for Xbox One powered by haptic technology.
HyperSense provides immersion in games and provides better control over the environment.
Razer HyperSense uses haptic solutions developed by Lofelt, a German company specializing in the development of advanced haptic technologies that provide a realistic touch-based experience.
HyperSense uses special haptic controllers and smart digital signal processing to generate high-resolution touch feedback in real time, giving you the ability to fully immerse yourself in any Xbox One game.
The technology recognizes sound signals and transforms them into dynamic vibrations, so that players can empathize with the gameplay without having to install additional software.
Thanks to the use of the sense of touch, sound signals can accurately mimic actions in the game.
Razer HyperSense recreates events – from quiet steps to powerful explosions, filing precisely all activities in the player’s environment.
“Nari Ultimate for Xbox One is designed to give all players an extra gameplay dimension.
With HyperSense, we allow them to completely immerse themselves in their favorite titles," said Alvin Cheung Senior Vice President on Razer peripherals.
Rotary earmuffs are equipped with cushions filled with foam with shape memory and a layer of cooling gel, in order to reduce the heat generated during long use.
For even easier operation of headphones, a quick mute button is placed on the retractable microphone, and HyperSense operating intensity regulator and the balance slider between the game and the chat.
Self-adapting to the shape of the headband for a trouble-free and accurate fit.
In addition, Razer Nari Ultimate for Xbox One features an Xbox Wireless feature that allows you to connect directly to your console without the need for a wireless transceiving device, allowing for an easy and fast configuration.
The headphones also support Windows Sonic, providing more realistic sound.
Razer Nari Ultimate, originally designed for PC, debuted on the market in September 2018.
With Nari Ultimate for Xbox One, Razer can now offer this award-winning technology to Xbox One fans.
The set was valued at 219.99 euros.
Someone shot a swan from a windbreaker
In the pond in Zameczno in Lower Silesia, residents noticed a swan having problems with its wings.
After fishing and visiting the veterinarian, it turned out that someone had arranged a target from the animal – in his body was found shot from a windbreaker.
“He received information about the injured bird from the inhabitants of the village of the Wildlife Rehabilitation Center in Nowa Sola.
It was clear from the report that the animal had broken wings.
We went to the scene.
It was immediately apparent that something was very wrong with him.
We acted quickly and precisely, so as not to hurt him and not expose him to additional stress.
The swan was caught and taken to a veterinarian.
After the first X-ray, it was already known that someone had made a shooting shield out of it.
There were debris in his body," says Marcin Walasek, the president of Malpol's company, which manages m.in. the rehabilitation center.
He's wintering at the facility
“Wounds have been cleared, antibiotics have been given to the bird, access to water was ensured, a safe place in the center where he will spend the entire winter.
We're trying to strengthen it.
For now, he's unable to fly.
Letting it out now would involve the fact that he most likely wouldn't survive the winter," adds Walasek.
Staff, after undergoing a swan rehabilitation, intend to release him into the same pond in the spring.
After receiving information about the cause of ill-health of the animal, they intend to inform the prosecutor’s office about the case.
The incident happened in Zameczno
Gowin: “we have to stimulate Polish, small trade”
“Effective taxation of hypermarkets does not solve the problem of minor trading, it will be necessary to consider whether the state has any instruments to stimulate Polish trading,” the deputy prime minister, minister of science and higher education, leader of the Jarosław Gowin Agreement, said on Friday.
Gowin, during a conversation in “Signals of the Day” in the Radio One, stated that trade is dominated by international networks, which impose such low margins on Polish producers that Polish companies actually cannot develop.
Noting that it is very difficult to fight this problem, the deputy prime minister reminded that the PiS government tried to face it at the very beginning of the term of office, but got a “counter from the EC”.
“We won in front of the tribunal of justice, and I hope that if the United Right wins the next election and formulates the government, we’ll go back to that,” he said.
At the same time, he pointed out that “efficient taxation of hypermarkets does not solve the problem of Polish, i.e. small trade”.
“We will have to think about whether the government, the state has any instruments to stimulate Polish trade,” Gowin said.
In May, an EU court decided that the European Commission had made a mistake in recognizing that the Polish retail sales tax was not allowed public aid.
The Act on Retail Sales Tax assumed the introduction of two trade tax rates: 0.8 percent on revenue between 17 million zlotys and 170 million zlotys per month and 1.4 percent on income above 170 million zlotys per month.
The tax was supposed to apply from September 2016.
In September 2016, the European Commission initiated proceedings for violations of EU law by Poland.
Brussels argued at the time that the construction of the tax could favour smaller stores, which could be considered public aid.
She then stated that the tribute had been implemented unlawfully.
It also issued an order to suspend the application of the tax pending the completion of its analysis by officials in Brussels.
Poland did not agree with this position, but the collection of the tax was suspended.
The EU court's May decision opened the way for a re-introduction of the tax, but it didn't finish the case.
On July 24, the Commission filed an appeal with the Court of Justice.
On Thursday, the CJEU’s press service told PAP that the case is currently at a written stage in which both the European Commission and the Polish government present their arguments in writing.
It is not yet known if and when the oral procedure will start, i.e. the hearing of the parties and a possible hearing.
It takes a good few to several months to file an appeal to announce the verdict.
"Such conduct lasts an average of one year," a source at the Luxembourg Court told PAP.
How to dress a child for baptism?
We provide some practical solutions
Baptism is an extremely important celebration in the life of an infant and his parents.
It is often the first opportunity at which the whole family gathers around the child, together celebrating its appearance in the world.
So it's not surprising that a fresh-faced mom and dad want their comfort to look their best on this day.
However, before you make a final decision about your child’s outfit, consider whether it will also be comfortable.
In stores you can find many tuning sets that do not provide the toddler with proper comfort.
So, what should you pay attention to?
The basic criterion for choosing clothes for baptism is the age of the child
Until recently, a few-week-old toddlers were baptized, tuned into white sets and inserted into the same beetles or great pillows.
Today, children entering the sacrament are often older: several months, annual and even larger.
It is not difficult to guess that such a big child already needs a slightly different clothes for baptism.
Therefore, if your children will be 3-4 months old on the day of baptism, he will probably spend the ceremony in a stroller or on the hands of parents or godparents.
The best solution will therefore be to decorate it with comfortable, cotton sleepers or sets.
Although this element of the wardrobe is considered an everyday outfit, it is enough to search for its festive variants, for example with frills or lace.
For the boy, it will be ideal to print bodies and suspenders.
In the case of older children, you can afford a greater fantasy in clothing.
The girl will look beautiful in a simple, tulle dress
Many of the girls' parents are longingly looking towards richly decorated, frolky dresses for baptism complete with coats, wristbands and hats.
Unfortunately, a large number of manufacturers use artificial, non-breathing materials for their production, in which the child is simply uncomfortable.
In search of the right clothes, it will be better to take a look at the Asanti for Kids store, which offers elegant outfits on cotton linings.
Delicate, tulle skirts, satin dresses, laces, applications and cute sets will make your daughter look lovely and comfortable.
The perfect outfit for a small gentleman: a cotton suit
Until recently, among the boys' parents there was a fashion for suits that were a copy of "adult" models.
Polyester jackets and trousers, stiff collars or caskets often made young elegants loudly demonstrate their dissatisfaction.
Today, fortunately, they have been replaced by comfortable, cotton sets.
Just look at the sets available in Asanti for Kids, i.e
These costumes look extremely festive, and at the same time they do not restrain the movements of the toddler.
Krystyna Pawłowicz published a property statement
Krystyna Pawłowicz made a property statement at the end of her term.
It shows that PiS has accumulated 110 thousand zlotys of savings.
Pawłowicz announced her departure from politics.
Concluding the term, he has an amount of 110 thousand zlotys
According to the statement made by the MP, she collects a pension with a monthly value of 4.7 thousand PLN.
Pawłowicz has an apartment worth 570 thousand zlotys and slightly smaller, which he rents, collecting 880 zlotys per month.
She also invests in industrial metals, valuing the investment at 150 thousand PLN.
